      "19316": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "bug_id": 19316,
            "text": "begincontext() calls R_BCRelPC() and vmaxget() while its seven arguments are still live, so they are saved around those calls on every closure call. Also, vmaxget() and vmaxset() are out-of-line calls even inside R, including in per-element loops such as the string hashing in unique.c.\n\nTimings: context-setup-vmax-bench.R, attached, prints ns per call or per element for four cases. On aarch64 macOS (Apple clang 21, r90887), an empty closure call is about 9% faster, and duplicated() and match() on UTF-8 strings about 10%.\n\nProposed patch: attached as context-setup-vmax-inline.diff, against r90887. begincontext() stores its arguments first and calls the accessors last. A file linked into R itself can define INLINE_VMAX before including Defn.h to get inline vmaxget() and vmaxset(); context.c and unique.c do. R_VStack becomes a hidden global (with an Rdll.hide entry), so nothing new is exported and packages keep calling the functions. Files that do not opt in are unaffected; eval.c compiles to the same instructions as before.\n\nmake check passes on macOS, and CI passes on Linux, macOS and Windows. The patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/488, with the full measurements.",
